## PART B · CL2 TOOLING: #84 and #140 (code branch for #84 only; #140 is outside the code repo)
**#84 (BACKLOG row 84, MEASURED text):** `scripts/up.sh` on a FRESH compose project printed `HEALTH: RED` because the host-side edge checks (`/api/healthz`, `/idp/healthz`, `/idp/.well-known/openid-configuration`) answered HTTP 000 straight after `compose up --wait`, while every container was healthy; a minute later all three gave 200. Seen once (B42, 2026-10-02, project `pc-b42base`, edge 19422). Fix-shape in the row: retry the host-side edge checks for a few seconds before RED. Files: `scripts/up.sh` and `scripts/health-check.sh` (MEASURED: both exist in the stale checkout; read them at `origin/main`).
- **Done when (drafter's, labelled so; Tuesday may replace):** (1) the three host-side edge checks are retried for a bounded time `@SLOT:RETRY_SECONDS@` seconds (default proposal 30) at a fixed interval before the script prints `HEALTH: RED`; (2) a check that never succeeds still ends RED, within the bound plus one interval, with the last HTTP code printed; (3) a check that fails twice and then succeeds ends GREEN, and the log says how many tries it took; (4) a container-level failure (not the edge race) is never retried away: it is RED at once; (5) there is a shell test, in the style of the repo's existing `scripts/*-test.sh` files, that proves (2), (3) and (4) with a stub `curl` earlier on `PATH` and a stubbed clock or a bound of 2 s, with its negative control (the old code fails (3)); (6) `scripts/ci.sh` runs the new test as a step (its summary count rises by one; B152's head was 20/20 GREEN, RELAYED), and `scripts/ci.sh` is run once end to end with the new count, GREEN.
- **PRIOR WORK first:** B42's evidence `Briefs/2026-10-02_B42_evidence/logs/up_base_proof.log` (named in the row); `git log -S'HEALTH: RED' -- scripts`; any later retry already present in `up.sh` (the row may already be fixed by a later seat: if so, the ticket's answer is a records line, not a branch; say so).
- **Prove the race is real or say it is not:** the row says "seen once". Try `up.sh` on a fresh project name `pc-b277-fresh-1` on your port block up to 3 times BEFORE the change; record each outcome (RED or GREEN, with timings). If it never reproduces, the retry is proved by the stub test only; write "not reproduced in n tries" in FOUND. Do not claim the race fixed on the stub test alone.
- **No product code**: only the two scripts, the new test and the `ci.sh` step. A change to anything else stops the work and goes to STATUS.
**#140 (BACKLOG row 140, MEASURED text):** the token checker `Briefs/2026-10-03_B47_evidence/b47-check-off-guide.cjs` (MEASURED: file exists; it is NOT in the code repo) strips `/* */` comments but not `//`, so "BACKLOG #114" in a `//` comment in `FeedbackWidget.tsx:341` (B51b) reads as a hex colour and every run since B51b reports "TOTAL off-guide: 1" with 0 computed.
- **Do:** leave the original byte-intact (it is B47's evidence). Write the fixed checker as a NEW file in `Briefs/2026-10-19_B277_evidence/b47-check-off-guide.v2.cjs`: strip `//` line comments in the TS/TSX static scan without damaging `//` inside string literals, template literals or URLs (`https://…`), plus a self-test mode with at least these cases, each with an expected result: `//` comment containing "#114" (not counted); the same text outside a comment (counted); `"https://x/#abc"` in a string (counted as the string content it is, not stripped); a `/* */` block (still stripped). Run both the old and the new checker over the same tree at `origin/main`: the old reads "TOTAL off-guide: 1", the new must read 0 where `FeedbackWidget.tsx:341` is the only cause. Quote both outputs. If the old reads something other than 1 at the current tree, say what it reads and why (row 140 says 1 at B51b).
- This is an evidence tool, not shipped code: no PR for it. It is listed under the records commit (`records/b277`) and the BACKLOG #140 State text is updated to cite the v2 file path, by the same CL0 rules.
